{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/qdor6d4b","slide":1,"name":"intro_body","text":"Micro-displacement inspection requires image features that can be located consistently when the objective changes. Optical blur and pixel sampling affect the boundary signals used to estimate position.\n\nMOSR combines calibrated optical guidance, anti-aliased multiscale features [1,2] and bounded correction on the original pixel grid. One fixed set of reconstruction weights serves 20× and 50×. We test its measurement benefit using the same circle-center procedure for Raw, fixed Wiener and MOSR.","textPreview":"Micro-displacement inspection requires image features that can be located consistently when the objective changes. Optical blur and pixel...","textChars":498,"textLines":3,"bbox":[123.03,1072.83,1456.69,383.86]}
