{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/y90nupkv","slide":1,"text":"IMPACT2026 TW0243. Public model name: MOSR. This poster presents an updated evaluation at a nominal 1 micrometer step. The 20x condition uses one complete 31-frame evaluation scan; the 50x condition uses its fixed prior list of 30 adjacent-frame pairs. Conditions are reported separately. All methods use the same image pairs, identities, scale and center-estimation procedure within each condition. Fig. 2 is a functional overview, not an isolated-component efficacy result. Fig. 3 uses measured boundary points and a fitted center from the displayed 20x MOSR field. The curves contain all 30 observed displacements per condition and method, minus nominal 1000 nm for display; no per-method centering, detrending or smoothing is applied. Sources for method context: Ronneberger et al., MICCAI 2015; Zhang, ICML 2019; Chan and Vese, IEEE TIP 2001; Chernov and Lesort, JMIV 2005."}